  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1215 AM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nA ridge axis associated with an Omega block is centered over \nthe southern Plains this morning, while sfc high pressure \nremains in control over the Great Lakes region. Radiational \ncooling will favor some patchy shallow ground fog, mainly near \nbodies of water where exceeding the crossover temperature will \nbe more probable. Otherwise, daily high temperatures today \nthrough Monday are progged around 5 degrees above normal as \nample sunshine is expected each day. As the omega block begins \nto break down, the ridge axis nudges more east over the FA by \nSaturday. Uncertainty in the synoptic details increases Tuesday\ninto Wednesday as the deterministic GFS was previously more \namplified with southern and northern stream energy phasing over \nthe Plains. Meanwhile, the ECMWF remains more progressive and \nzonal in line with the LREF, including the GEFS. Given meager \n700 mb moisture and questionable 500 mb forcing, only a 10-15% \nchance of a sprinkle Tuesday night into Wednesday will be \npossible as a cold front moves through, bringing more seasonable\ntemperatures.",
